UID:019dd4fb-ae21-2e16-f346-ad206ac21b04@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, July 8\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 13m\n\n1997 | 133 min. | Japan | Colo
 r | Japanese with English subtitles | Rated PG-13 | 35mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN
  BY: Hayao Miyazaki \nWITH: Yoji Matsuda\, Yuriko Ishida\, Yuko Tanaka\, 
 Kaoru Kobayashi\nNew subtitled print courtesy of the Academy Film Archive\
 , with special thanks to Studio Ghibli.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nHayao Miyaz
 aki’s international breakthrough is an epic cinematic marvel. Infected b
 y a deadly curse after killing a god\, young warrior Ashitaka heads west i
 n search of a cure. He stumbles upon a bitter conflict between Lady Eboshi
 \, the proud people of Iron Town\, and the enigmatic Princess Mononoke\, a
  girl raised by wolves and who will stop at nothing to prevent humans from
  destroying her home\, and the forest spirits and animal gods who live the
 re. Princess Mononoke resists an easy dichotomy of good versus evil and wa
 s the first Miyazaki film that incorporated computer-generated imagery alo
 ngside traditional hand-drawn animation.
