BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bugsy in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T223000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd52f-a256-6605-687a-101422312e89@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: producer Mark Johnson\, production designer Dennis 
 Gassner and Academy Governor Daniel Orlandi.\nSelected by the Costume Desi
 gners Branch\n\nWednesday\, July 15\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy
  Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 15m\n\n1991 | 135 min. | USA | C
 olor | English | Rated R | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Barry Levinson \nWRITTEN BY
 : James Toback \nWITH: Warren Beatty\, Annette Bening\, Harvey Keitel\, J
 oe Mantegna \nPrint courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screeni
 ngs\n\nOscar winner Barry Levinson (Rain Man\, 1988) directed this lavish 
 biographical gangster drama about the notorious Benjamin “Bugsy” Siege
 l (Best Actor nominee Warren Beatty)\, his romance with the beautiful Virg
 inia Hill (Annette Bening)\, and his role in the transformation of Las Veg
 as into a gambling mecca. The film earned 10 Oscar nominations\, including
  Best Picture\, Directing\, Original Screenplay\, Cinematography\, and the
  supporting performances of Harvey Keitel (as Mickey Cohen) and Ben Kingsl
 ey (as Meyer Lansky). Oscars were awarded for Art Direction (Dennis Gassne
 r\, Nancy Haigh) and the elegant\, expressive\, and period-perfect costume
  designs of two-time winner Albert Wolsky (All That Jazz\, 1979)
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/bugsy-019dd52f-a256-6
 605-687a-101422312e89
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Juice with Ernest Dickerson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T223000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd57f-69a3-8bdd-8d5a-ac677c12b91a@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, July 16\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 35m\n\n1992 | 95 min. | USA | Color |
  English | Rated R | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Ernest R. Dickerson \nWRITTEN BY
 : Ernest R. Dickerson\, Gerard Brown \nWITH: Omar Epps\, Tupac Shakur\, J
 ermaine Hopkins\, Khalil Kain\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe directorial debut
  of Ernest R. Dickerson\, who previously lensed Spike Lee’s Do The Right
  Thing (1989) and Malcolm X (1992)\, trains its sights on four Black teena
 gers in Harlem. While Q (Omar Epps) is obsessed with becoming a DJ and the
  “juice” it would bring to his reputation\, ringleader Raheem (Khalil 
 Kain) has bigger scores in mind. When a seemingly low-stakes bodega robber
 y goes awry\, bullied Bishop (Tupac Shakur) allows the allure of power and
  violence get to his head. Dickerson’s confident crime film is steeped i
 n neorealism and noir traditions and fuels its narrative with ‘90s hip-h
 op—Too $hort\, Salt-N-Pepa\, Fabulous Five Inc.\, Cypress Hill—buoyed 
 by an electric performance from Tupac Shakur.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/juice-with-ernest-dic
 kerson-019dd57f-69a3-8bdd-8d5a-ac677c12b91a
END:VEVENT
