BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poison Ivy in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T223000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd57f-e1cb-bdce-e97c-4a394e83a8eb@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: cinematographer Phedon Papamichael and director Kat
 t Shea\n\nFriday\, July 17\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum o
 f Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 33m\n\n1992 | 93 min. | USA | Color | Eng
 lish | Rated R | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Katt Shea Ruben \nWRITTEN BY: Andy Ru
 ben\, Katt Shea Ruben \nWITH: Tom Skerritt\, Sara Gilbert\, Cheryl Ladd\, 
 Drew Barrymore \nPrint courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Scre
 enings\n\nWith her dad experiencing a mid-life crisis and mom sick and bed
 -ridden\, Sylvie Cooper (Sara Gilbert) has resorted to lying and bomb thre
 ats to give her life meaning\, until she befriends the mysterious and sedu
 ctive Ivy (Drew Barrymore). Ivy easily infiltrates this dysfunctional fami
 ly\, and as her deceit and manipulation creates chaos and tragedy\, she sh
 atters this family to make a spot for herself. Filled with classic tropes 
 of the erotic thriller including a femme fatale\, illicit seduction\, and 
 murder\, Poison Ivy is often described as a teenage Fatal Attraction. It w
 ent on to spawn three direct-to-home-video sequels.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/poison-ivy-019dd57f-e
 1cb-bdce-e97c-4a394e83a8eb
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Great Mouse Detective
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T121500
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019db101-4c28-f4d0-d99e-71207761efa6@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, July 18\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 11m\n\n1986 | 71 min. | USA | Color | E
 nglish | Rated G | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Musker\, Ron Clements\, Dave Mi
 chener\, Burny Mattinson \nWRITTEN BY: Pete Young\, Vance Gerry\, Steve H
 ulett\, Ron Clements\, John Musker\, Bruce M. Morris\, Matthew O’Callagh
 an\, Burny Mattinson\, Dave Michener\, Melvin Shaw.  \nWITH: Vincent Pric
 e\, Barrie Ingham\, Val Bettin\, Alan Young\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA mouse
  living in the cellar of Sherlock Holmes’s house is himself a brilliant 
 detective in this mystery inspired by the Basil of Baker Street books by E
 ve Titus and Paul Galdone. Four directors collaborated on this charming an
 imated feature\, including Disney veteran Burny Mattinson and the team of 
 John Musker and Ron Clements (The Little Mermaid\, 1989\, Aladdin\, 1992)\
 , while Vincent Price loaned his unmistakable voice to the evil Professor 
 Ratigan. The lighthearted score was composed by four-time Oscar winner Hen
 ry Mancini\, his first for an animated feature.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-great-mouse-detec
 tive-019db101-4c28-f4d0-d99e-71207761efa6
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:30th Anniversary of From Dusk Till Dawn with Robert Rodriguez\, pl
 us a performance by Robert Rodriguez's CHINGON BAND
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T223000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019db1fc-f863-def8-3638-c35bc75970cc@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Robert Rodriguez\n\nSaturday\, July 18\, 2026 at 7 
 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 48m\n\n19
 96. 108 min. USA. Color. English. Rated R. DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Robert Rodri
 guez  \nWRITTEN BY: Quentin Tarantino \nSTORY BY: Robert Kurtzman \nWITH
 : Harvey Keitel\, George Clooney\, Quentin Tarantino\, Juliette Lewis\n\nT
 ype: Screenings\n\nAfter establishing himself as a cinematic powerhouse wi
 th his successful indie action film El Mariachi (1992) and its studio-back
 ed sequel\, Desperado (1995)\, Robert Rodriguez upped the ante with his ne
 xt feature\, introducing horror elements to his world of stylish\, neo-wes
 tern action films. Violent fugitives the Gecko brothers (portrayed by Geor
 ge Clooney and the film’s screenwriter\, Quentin Tarantino)\, take a wid
 owed pastor (Harvey Keitel) and his teen children hostage\, hoping to cros
 s the Mexican border undetected. Ending up in a saloon full of exotic danc
 ers and rowdy bikers\, the group is confronted by an ancient evil\, spurri
 ng an all-night fight for survival. Featuring supporting roles by Cheech M
 arin\, Fred Williamson\, and Salma Hayek\, From Dusk Till Dawn is a riotou
 s thrill ride packed with gunslinging action and vampire violence that has
  gone on to achieve cult status\, continuing to keep fans partying all nig
 ht long. \nThis program begins with a screening\, followed by a conversat
 ion with filmmaker Robert Rodriguez and a live performance from his band.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/30th-anniversary-of-f
 rom-dusk-till-dawn-with-robert-rodriguez-019db1fc-f863-def8-3638-c35bc7597
 0cc
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fantômas Episodes 1-5
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T150000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd580-a360-5491-7f1f-62166fa72be4@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, July 19\, 2026 at 12 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum o
 f Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 5h 20m\n\n1913-14 | 320 min. | France | Blac
 k-and-White | French | Not Rated | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Louis Feuilla
 de \nWITH: René Navarre\, Edmund Breon\, Georges Melchior\, Renée Carl\
 n\nType: Screenings\n\nA form most popular in the early 20th century\, a f
 ilm serial is a story told over a sequence of short episodes\, with each p
 iece intended to be viewed before a feature-length film. These bite-size p
 rograms were presented weekly in chronological order\, adding entertainmen
 t and value to a program\, and were a common component of the filmgoing ex
 perience through the 1940s. A gripping crime thriller showcasing stunning 
 visual compositions and production design\, Fantômas is a five-part episo
 dic serial based on the novel of the same name by Marcel Allain and Pierre
  Souvestre. Set in Paris\, the series follows a manhunt by Inspector Juve 
 (Edmund Breon) for Fantômas (René Navarre)\, an infamous criminal who is
  also a master of disguise\, completely his victims and the authorities.\n
 The schedule of breaks will be posted closer to showtime.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/fantomas-e-1-5-019dd5
 80-a360-5491-7f1f-62166fa72be4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:25th Anniversary of Spy Kids with Robert Rodriguez\, plus a perfor
 mance by The Rodriguez Family SPY BAND
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T163000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019db1ff-c1d7-27a3-7600-c9e6b670fc82@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Robert Rodriguez\n\nSunday\, July 19\, 2026 at 2 pm
 \n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 28m\n\n2001
 . 88 min. USA. Color. English. Rated PG. DCP \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Rober
 t Rodriguez \nWITH: Antonio Banderas\, Carla Gugino\, Alexa PenaVega\, Da
 ryl Sabara\n\nType: Screenings\n\nCarmen (Alexa PenaVega) and Juni Cortez 
 (Daryl Sabara) come from a normal\, boring family. They deal with everyday
  problems\, such as school bullies and warts\, until they discover their p
 arents\, Gregorio (Antonio Banderas) and Ingrid (Carla Gugino)\, are secre
 t agents who have been captured by an evil television host\, Fegan Floop (
 Alan Cumming). Carmen and Juni must overcome their fears and work together
  to save their parents and\, ultimately\, the world. Robert Rodriguez’s 
 Spy Kids is an epic kid-power fantasy blending the action of James Bond wi
 th the whimsy of Willy Wonka in a film that feels straight from the mind o
 f a child. Filled with fantastical characters\, mutated creatures\, and in
 ventive gadgets\, this enduring children’s classic sparked a vast franch
 ise and was added to the United States National Film Registry in 2024. \n
 This program begins with a screening\, followed by a conversation with fil
 mmaker Robert Rodriguez and a live performance from his band.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/25th-anniversary-of-s
 py-kids-with-robert-rodriguez-019db1ff-c1d7-27a3-7600-c9e6b670fc82
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spirited Away in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260720T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260720T150000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd515-2d0b-9831-de23-02777c0d6b0c@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, July 20\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 5m\n\n2001 | 125 min. | Japan | Color |
  Japanese with English subtitles | Rated PG | 35mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: H
 ayao Miyazaki \nWITH: Rumi Hiiragi\, Miyu Irino\, Mari Natsuki\, Takashi 
 Naito \nNew subtitled print courtesy of the Academy Film Archive\, with sp
 ecial thanks to Studio Ghibli.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nSpirited Away was Ha
 yao Miyazaki’s first Oscar win\, and the first hand-drawn\, non-English-
 language animated film to win the Academy Award for Best Animated Feature.
  The film invites audiences into a mind-bending supernatural realm when a 
 wrong turn on a family road trip lands 10-year-old Chihiro in a mysterious
  dimension populated by all manner of creatures\, including soot gremlins 
 (first introduced in My Neighbor Totoro)\, the giant witch Yubaba\, and\, 
 most memorably\, the enigmatic No Face. To find her parents and return to 
 the real world\, Chihiro must work at an enchanted bathhouse serving spiri
 ts of all shapes and sizes. A tour de force of surrealist invention\, Spir
 ited Away is a timeless wonder filled with whimsy and joy.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/spirited-away-019dd51
 5-2d0b-9831-de23-02777c0d6b0c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Le Cercle Rouge in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260720T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260720T223000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd581-418a-70dd-ff2c-889ba35b3859@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, July 20\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 20m\n\n1970 | 140 min. | France | Color
  | French | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Jean-Pierre Melville \nWRITT
 EN BY: Jean-Pierre Melville \nWITH: Alain Delon\, André Bourvil\, Gian Ma
 ria Volontè\, Yves Montand\n\nType: Screenings\n\nMaster of French crime 
 thrillers Jean-Pierre Melville landed this gangster epic toward the end of
  his filmography\, before his sudden death at 55. Dense\, atmospheric comp
 onents of neo noir amplify a stoic persona elegantly delivered by Alain De
 lon in his portrayal of master thief Corey. Along with infamous prison esc
 apee Vogel and troubled ex-cop Jansen\, he plans a jewelry heist so risky 
 as to assume the three are doomed\, perhaps even to death. Eventually comp
 assion and friendship bloom —the epitome of balance.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/le-cercle-rouge-019dd
 581-418a-70dd-ff2c-889ba35b3859
END:VEVENT
