SUMMARY:Spirited Away in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T150000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd515-b15a-7db7-ab67-8c426be3b0bf@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, July 22\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 5m\n\n2001 | 125 min. | Japan | Colo
 r | Japanese with English subtitles | Rated PG | 35mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY
 : Hayao Miyazaki \nWITH: Rumi Hiiragi\, Miyu Irino\, Mari Natsuki\, Takas
 hi Naito \nNew subtitled print courtesy of the Academy Film Archive\, with
  special thanks to Studio Ghibli.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nSpirited Away was
  Hayao Miyazaki’s first Oscar win\, and the first hand-drawn\, non-Engli
 sh-language animated film to win the Academy Award for Best Animated Featu
 re. The film invites audiences into a mind-bending supernatural realm when
  a wrong turn on a family road trip lands 10-year-old Chihiro in a mysteri
 ous dimension populated by all manner of creatures\, including soot gremli
 ns (first introduced in My Neighbor Totoro)\, the giant witch Yubaba\, and
 \, most memorably\, the enigmatic No Face. To find her parents and return 
 to the real world\, Chihiro must work at an enchanted bathhouse serving sp
 irits of all shapes and sizes. A tour de force of surrealist invention\, S
 pirited Away is a timeless wonder filled with whimsy and joy.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
