BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Titicut Follies in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260805T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260805T223000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd531-3419-7f41-baa2-1ec05eb4f02f@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Academy Governor Kate Amend\nSelected by the Docume
 ntary Branch\n\nWednesday\, August 5\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academ
 y Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 27m\n\n1967 | 87 min. | USA | B
 lack-and-White | English | 4K DCP\nDIRECTED BY: Frederick Wiseman\n\nType:
  Screenings\n\nFilmmaker Frederick Wiseman spent 29 days in 1966 at the Br
 idgewater State Hospital in Massachusetts\, filming the treatment and mist
 reatment of its patients. After a year of editing\, the result\, the first
  feature from the noted documentarian\, established his distinctively obse
 rvational filmmaking style. Banned from public exhibition for decades and 
 finally approved for release on First Amendment grounds in a 1991 court de
 cision\, Titicut Follies was selected for preservation by the National Fil
 m Registry in 2022. In 2016\, Wiseman—whose other classic documentaries 
 include High School (1968)\, Primate (1974) and Welfare (1975)— received
  an honorary Oscar for his “masterful and distinctive documentaries [tha
 t] examine the familiar and reveal the unexpected.”
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/titicut-falls-019dd53
 1-3419-7f41-baa2-1ec05eb4f02f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In the Cut in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260806T223000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd585-40b8-73e6-0781-56750aa09dd3@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, August 6\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 59m\n\n2003 | 119 min. | USA | Color
  | English | Rated R | 35mm\nDIRECTED BY: Jane Campion \nWRITTEN BY: Jane
  Campion\, Susanna Moore \nWITH: Meg Ryan\, Mark Ruffalo\, Jennifer Jason
  Leigh\, Kevin Bacon\n\nType: Screenings\n\nJane Campion’s gritty erotic
  thriller stars Meg Ryan as Frannie Avery\, a seemingly apathetic writer a
 nd English teacher who finds solace in her daydream of language and litera
 ture. At a bar near her apartment\, Frannie accidentally witnesses a sexua
 l encounter between a woman and a man whose face she cannot recall. The wo
 man is later found dismembered\, spurring a visit from a detective who qui
 ckly becomes Frannie’s infatuation. Paralleling the desolate ambience of
  the urban landscape is Frannie’s facade\, until her suppressed emotions
  trigger outbursts that may lead her straight into the path of a serial ki
 ller of women.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/in-the-cut-019dd585-4
 0b8-73e6-0781-56750aa09dd3
END:VEVENT
