BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:To Be or Not to Be
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260812T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260812T223000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd531-8cec-e732-df70-044dfc38219b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Executives Branch\n\nWednesday\, August 12\, 2
 026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 
 1h 40m\n\n1942 | 100 min. | USA | Black-and-White | English | DCP\nDIRECTE
 D BY: Ernst Lubitsch \nWRITTEN BY: Edwin Justus Mayer \nSTORY BY: Melchior
  Lengyel \nWITH: Carole Lombard\, Jack Benny\, Robert Stack\, Felix Bressa
 rt\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA Shakespearean actor reluctantly joins a Resist
 ance plot against the Nazis in 1939 Warsaw in this daring comedy directed 
 by two-time Oscar nominee Ernst Lubitsch (Heaven Can Wait\, 1943). Comedy 
 legend Jack Benny had his greatest screen role as the pompous ham Joseph T
 ura\, and Oscar nominee Carole Lombard (My Man Godfrey\, 1936) was his exp
 ert match as his actress wife\, Maria\, her final film role before her dea
 th weeks before the film’s release. Finding the perfect balance between 
 wartime tension and hilarious farce\, Lubitsch’s classic— filmed right
  as the U.S. entered World War II— was remade in 1983\, with Mel Brooks 
 and Anne Bancroft as the couple.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/to-be-or-not-to-be-01
 9dd531-8cec-e732-df70-044dfc38219b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fatal Attraction with Adrian Lyne
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T223000
DTSTAMP:20260704T101017Z
UID:019dd58c-f37f-8692-e2f3-b2c358295fda@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: director Adrian Lyne\n\nThursday\, August 13\, 2026
  at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 
 59m\n\n1987 | 119 min. | USA | Color | English | Rated R | 4K DCP\nDIRECTE
 D BY: Adrian Lyne \nWRITTEN BY: James Dearden \nWITH: Michael Douglas\, 
 Glenn Close\, Anne Archer\, Ellen Hamilton Latzen\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA
 drian Lyne’s groundbreaking 1987 erotic thriller\, which garnered six Os
 car nominations\, contributed to the phenomenal boom of this subgenre\, an
 d it remains iconic and timeless. Glenn Close is compelling in her portray
 al of Alex\, a book editor who has an affair with Dan (Michael Douglas)\, 
 a happily married attorney whose life becomes an unbearable torture after 
 the tryst. Passion turns into obsession\; Alex not only terrorizes Dan but
  also his wife and young daughter. Close’s deep dive into Alex’s psych
 ological state\, exhibited in the extreme measures she takes to possess Da
 n\, is manifested in an intense performance\,and the chemistry she shares 
 with Douglas’s riveting Dan creates simultaneously repulsive and magneti
 c dynamics between them.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/fatal-attraction-019d
 d58c-f37f-8692-e2f3-b2c358295fda
END:VEVENT
